{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Records","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence ends once the tracker’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/finish()"},{"type":"text","text":" is called, or its every copy is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"released, and every record before it has been read. Records tracked while nothing is reading wait in memory, without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound, for the next read, so none tracked before a delivery starts, or between two, is lost."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A read whose task is cancelled returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and takes nothing: the next read gets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record it was waiting for, and every one after. A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/noOp"},{"type":"text","text":" tracker’s records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One task reads at a time, as with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":": calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" while another task’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call is waiting traps. A reader that has been cancelled stops waiting as its cancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches it, so start a new delivery once the cancelled one’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"execute()"},{"type":"text","text":" has returned."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The records of the events a tracker tracks, in the order tracked: what a delivery reads.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Trackers\/Sci"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncIterator"],"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/makeAsyncIterator()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/Element","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/Failure"],"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/Records-swift.struct\/AsyncSequence-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackers\/tracker\/records-swift.struct"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Trackers\/Records.swift#L23","fileName":"Records.swift"},"title":"Tracker.Records","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Records","kind":"iden